# SYNTHETIC Born effective charges for the CO2 fixture - not from a DFT run.
# Magnitudes are representative of a covalent triatomic; what matters physically is
# that they respect the two hard constraints:
#   1. D_inf_h site symmetry: every tensor is diagonal with Z_xx = Z_yy != Z_zz,
#      and the two oxygens are related by the inversion centre so their tensors are
#      identical (Z* is even under inversion).
#   2. Acoustic sum rule: Z*(C) + 2 Z*(O) = 0 exactly.
# The symmetry-forced zero IR intensities of the gerade modes follow from these
# constraints alone and are independent of the magnitudes chosen.
# Line 1 = NAC unit conversion factor, line 2 = dielectric tensor, then one tensor/atom.
14.400
1.15000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 1.15000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 1.30000000
0.60000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.60000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 1.30000000
-0.30000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 -0.30000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 -0.65000000
-0.30000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 -0.30000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 0.00000000 -0.65000000
